.TH SPORTS-GAME 1 "2026-09-13" "sports_near_me 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sports-game \- show when a followed team plays next, and how to watch or listen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sports-game
.RI [ shared-options ]
.RI [ sport
.RI [ team ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sports-game
looks up a team's next scheduled game (or a specific numbered week, or
every game in a rolling day window) from ESPN's public schedule data and
prints when the data was fetched, kickoff time, venue, and how the game
is broadcast \(em television/streaming and audio, reported separately,
plus a direct link to the game's ESPN page.
.PP
It covers ten leagues: NFL, MLB, NHL, NCAA football, NCAA men's and
women's basketball, NCAA baseball, NCAA men's hockey, and NCAA men's and
women's volleyball.
.PP
Run with a
.I sport
and
.I team
for one specific lookup. Run with just a
.I sport
to show every team (and every team in every followed conference) from
your config file's follow list for that sport. Run with
.B no arguments at all
to show your entire follow list across every sport.
.PP
Team names resolve loosely: a nickname, city, full team name, or league
abbreviation all work (\fBbears\fR, \fBchicago\fR, \fB"chicago bears"\fR,
\fBCHI\fR are all the Chicago Bears). A name that matches more than one
team \(em e.g. \fBnew york\fR, which is both the Giants and the Jets \(em
is refused with the list of real matches rather than guessed at.
.SH SPORTS
.TP
.B nfl
National Football League
.TP
.B mlb
Major League Baseball. The only league where ESPN reports the real
National/Home/Away broadcast split per game \(em see
.B BROADCAST NOTES
below.
.TP
.B nhl
National Hockey League
.TP
.B ncaaf
NCAA football
.TP
.B ncaamb
NCAA men's basketball
.TP
.B ncaawb
NCAA women's basketball
.TP
.B ncaabsb
NCAA baseball
.TP
.B ncaamh
NCAA men's hockey
.TP
.B ncaavbw
NCAA women's volleyball
.TP
.B ncaavbm
NCAA men's volleyball
.PP
Every NCAA sport supports following a whole conference (see
.BR sports_near_me.yaml (5))
\(em team and conference names for NCAA sports are resolved against
ESPN's live team/conference lists on every run, not a hardcoded table,
since a handful of hundred-plus-school sports would be impractical to
hand-maintain and conference realignment does happen.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Path to a YAML config file. Default: \fI~/.sports_near_me.yaml\fR if it
exists; if omitted and no default file exists, only explicit
.I sport team
lookups work \(em there is no follow list to fall back to.
.TP
.BI \-\-week " N"
Show a specific numbered week's game instead of the next upcoming one.
Only meaningful for \fBnfl\fR and \fBncaaf\fR, which carry week numbers;
other sports ignore it. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-range .
.TP
.BI \-\-range " Nd"
Show every game in a rolling window starting today \(em
.B 1d
is today only (including games already finished earlier today),
.B 7d
is the next 7 days. By calendar date in the display timezone (see
.BR \-\-tz ).
Can return more than one game for sports that play daily, e.g. MLB.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-week .
.TP
.BI \-\-tz " zone"
IANA timezone for the printed kickoff time (e.g.
.IR America/Chicago ).
Default:
.B "this machine's local timezone"
\(em the zone actually used is always shown (e.g.
.IR EDT ),
never hidden. Set this if you want a specific zone regardless of what
machine runs the command \(em useful if a config file gets shared and run
somewhere else, or to make
.BR \-\-range 's
day boundaries match a different calendar day.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-dir " dir"
Also write a timestamped diagnostic log file under
.I dir
(created if needed), in addition to stderr. Diagnostics never appear in
the report itself (stdout).
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
One of \fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR,
\fBCRITICAL\fR. Default: \fBINFO\fR. Mutually exclusive with
.B \-\-verbose
and
.BR \-\-silent .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Shortcut for \fB\-\-log\-level DEBUG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Shortcut for \fB\-\-log\-level ERROR\fR \(em only the report and real
errors are printed.
.SH AS-OF TIMESTAMP
Every run prints an
.B "As of:"
line before any game reports, in the display timezone. Schedules are not
static \(em weather postponements, doubleheaders, and flexed games can
all change a schedule after this data was fetched \(em so this is what
tells you how fresh the report is.
.SH BROADCAST NOTES
The
.B TV
line and
.B Audio
line are always printed separately, whatever ESPN reports for the game
\(em called
.B Audio ,
not
.IR Radio ,
since most of what is listed here is consumed as internet audio today
(team apps, TuneIn), not strictly an AM/FM signal. A
.B "More at:"
line follows with a direct link to the game's ESPN Gamecast page, when
ESPN provides one \(em true for every league checked so far.
Classification differs by league because the underlying broadcast
systems genuinely differ:
.TP
.B NFL
Flagship windows and streaming exclusives (NBC, ESPN/ABC, Prime Video,
NFL Network, Peacock, Netflix) are flagged as reaching every market.
FOX/CBS Sunday-window games cannot be resolved to a specific market by
this tool \(em that depends on affiliate coverage maps that
.B sports-game
has no access to (the sites that publish them block automated
requests). The note instead points to a real, verified county/zip-
searchable coverage map at
.IR https://thesportsmaps.com/nfl/ ,
or the NFL app's "Local" tab.
.TP
.B MLB
ESPN reports the actual National/Home/Away split per game, so
.B sports-game
prints all of it directly \(em e.g. national streaming on MLB.TV plus
each team's own regional network. A note about MLB.TV's blackout of
both teams' home markets is appended when relevant.
.TP
.B NCAA (all six sports) and NHL national games
A conference or league TV/streaming deal is one single
nationally-distributed feed of that specific game, not a regional split
\(em you just need the matching cable/streaming access.
.TP
.B NHL non-national games
ESPN's schedule data does not include regional-sports-network coverage
for most NHL games; an empty broadcast line there means "check your
team's local RSN or streaming app," not "nothing airs."
.TP
.B Audio, specifically
ESPN's own audio data is confirmed incomplete \(em a real Bears game
came back with zero audio entries despite WBBM actively carrying every
Bears game under a standing contract \(em so an empty
.B Audio
line is a hedge, not a flat "nothing airs." Two more lines follow when
known: a
.B "Verified regional flagship"
from a small, hand-checked table (Bears\(->WBBM, Cubs\(->WSCR,
Blackhawks\(->WGN, Tennessee football\(->the Vol Network \(em
deliberately partial, not a guess at every team), and
.B "Out-of-market listeners"
\(em each league's own standing national audio option(s), shown for
every game regardless of what ESPN reported (Westwood One + iHeartRadio
for NFL, MLB Audio + the official app for MLB, TuneIn for NHL) \(em each
checked for being both real
.I and
actually free where claimed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one game report was printed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
No team/sport was resolvable, the config file was invalid or missing
when explicitly requested, or nothing could be shown at all.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.sports_near_me.yaml
Default config file. See
.BR sports_near_me.yaml (5).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Look up one team directly:
.B sports-game nfl bears
.TP
A specific numbered week:
.B sports-game ncaaf "ohio state" \-\-week 3
.TP
Every game today, in a specific timezone:
.B sports-game mlb cubs \-\-range 1d \-\-tz America/Chicago
.TP
Every game in the next 7 days:
.B sports-game mlb cubs \-\-range 7d \-\-tz America/Chicago
.TP
Show every NCAA football team/conference you follow:
.B sports-game ncaaf
.TP
Show your entire follow list, every sport:
.B sports-game
.TP
Use a specific config file:
.B sports-game \-\-config ~/work/sports.yaml mlb cubs
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sports_near_me.yaml (5),
.BR sports-game-launchers (7)
.SH NOTES
No team or conference id is ever cached or written to disk \(em every
name is resolved fresh against ESPN's live data on each run. See
.I docs/EXTENDING.md
in the project source for why that matters and how to add another
league.
